    <interface name="AccessibleText"
               c:symbol-prefix="accessible_text"
               c:type="GtkAccessibleText"
               version="4.14"
               glib:type-name="GtkAccessibleText"
               glib:get-type="gtk_accessible_text_get_type"
               glib:type-struct="AccessibleTextInterface">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk/gtkaccessibletext.h"
           line="20">An interface for accessible objects containing formatted text.

The `GtkAccessibleText` interfaces is meant to be implemented by accessible
objects that have text formatted with attributes, or non-trivial text contents.

You should use the [enum@Gtk.AccessibleProperty.LABEL] or the
[enum@Gtk.AccessibleProperty.DESCRIPTION] properties for accessible
objects containing simple, unformatted text.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gtk/gtkaccessibletext.h" line="324"/>
      <prerequisite name="Accessible"/>
      <virtual-method name="get_attributes" version="4.14">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtkaccessibletext.h"
             line="191">Retrieves the text attributes inside the accessible object.

Each attribute is composed by:

- a range
- a name
- a value

It is left to the implementation to determine the serialization format
of the value to a string.

GTK provides support for various text attribute names and values, but
implementations of this interface are free to add their own attributes.

If this function returns true, `n_ranges` will be set to a value
greater than or equal to one, @ranges will be set to a newly
allocated array of [struct#Gtk.AccessibleTextRange].</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtkaccessibletext.h" line="226"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk/gtkaccessibletext.h"
               line="221">true if the accessible object has at least an attribute,
  and false otherwise</doc>
          <type name="gboolean" c:type="gboolean"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtkaccessibletext.h"
                 line="193">the accessible object</doc>
            <type name="AccessibleText" c:type="GtkAccessibleText*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
          <parameter name="offset" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtkaccessibletext.h"
                 line="194">the offset, in characters</doc>
            <type name="guint" c:type="unsigned int"/>
          </parameter>
          <parameter name="n_ranges"
                     direction="out"
