      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk/deprecated/gtkcolorbutton.c"
           line="51">The `GtkColorButton` allows to open a color chooser dialog to change
the color.

&lt;picture&gt;
  &lt;source srcset="color-button-dark.png" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"&gt;
  &lt;img alt="An example GtkColorButton" src="color-button.png"&gt;
&lt;/picture&gt;

It is suitable widget for selecting a color in a preference dialog.

# CSS nodes

```
colorbutton
╰── button.color
    ╰── [content]
```

`GtkColorButton` has a single CSS node with name colorbutton which
contains a button node. To differentiate it from a plain `GtkButton`,
it gets the .color style class.</doc>
