    <class name="ColumnViewCell"
           c:symbol-prefix="column_view_cell"
           c:type="GtkColumnViewCell"
           version="4.12"
           parent="ListItem"
           glib:type-name="GtkColumnViewCell"
           glib:get-type="gtk_column_view_cell_get_type"
           glib:type-struct="ColumnViewCellClass">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk/gtkcolumnviewcell.c"
           line="26">Represents items in a cell in [class@Gtk.ColumnView].

The `GtkColumnViewCell`s are managed by the [class@Gtk.ColumnView]
widget (with its factory) and cannot be created by applications, but
they need to be populated by application code. This is done by calling
[method@Gtk.ColumnViewCell.set_child].

`GtkColumnViewCell`s exist in 2 stages:

1. The unbound stage where the listitem is not currently connected to
   an item in the list. In that case, the [property@Gtk.ColumnViewCell:item]
   property is set to %NULL.

2. The bound stage where the listitem references an item from the list.
   The [property@Gtk.ColumnViewCell:item] property is not %NULL.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gtk/gtkcolumnviewcell.h" line="33"/>
      <method name="get_child"
              c:identifier="gtk_column_view_cell_get_child"
              glib:get-property="child"
