      <method name="set_markup" c:identifier="gtk_label_set_markup">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtklabel.c"
             line="3977">Sets the labels text and attributes from markup.

The string must be marked up with Pango markup
(see [func@Pango.parse_markup]).

If @str is external data, you may need to escape it
with [func@GLib.markup_escape_text] or [func@GLib.markup_printf_escaped]:

```c
GtkWidget *self = gtk_label_new (NULL);
const char *str = "...";
const char *format = "&lt;span style=\"italic\"&gt;\%s&lt;/span&gt;";
char *markup;

markup = g_markup_printf_escaped (format, str);
gtk_label_set_markup (GTK_LABEL (self), markup);
g_free (markup);
```

This function sets the [property@Gtk.Label:use-markup] property
to true.

Also see [method@Gtk.Label.set_text].</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtklabel.h" line="63"/>
