    <class name="ListItem"
           c:symbol-prefix="list_item"
           c:type="GtkListItem"
           parent="GObject.Object"
           glib:type-name="GtkListItem"
           glib:get-type="gtk_list_item_get_type"
           glib:type-struct="ListItemClass">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk/gtklistitem.c"
           line="27">Used by list widgets to represent items in a [iface@Gio.ListModel].

`GtkListItem` objects are managed by the list widget (with its factory)
and cannot be created by applications, but they need to be populated
by application code. This is done by calling [method@Gtk.ListItem.set_child].

`GtkListItem` objects exist in 2 stages:

1. The unbound stage where the listitem is not currently connected to
   an item in the list. In that case, the [property@Gtk.ListItem:item]
   property is set to `NULL`.

2. The bound stage where the listitem references an item from the list.
   The [property@Gtk.ListItem:item] property is not `NULL`.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gtk/gtklistitem.h" line="32"/>
