    <interface name="Root"
               c:symbol-prefix="root"
               c:type="GtkRoot"
               glib:type-name="GtkRoot"
               glib:get-type="gtk_root_get_type"
               glib:type-struct="RootInterface">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk/gtkroot.c"
           line="32">An interface for widgets that can act as the root of a widget hierarchy.

The root widget takes care of providing the connection to the windowing
system and manages layout, drawing and event delivery for its widget
hierarchy.

The obvious example of a `GtkRoot` is `GtkWindow`.

To get the display to which a `GtkRoot` belongs, use
[method@Gtk.Root.get_display].

`GtkRoot` also maintains the location of keyboard focus inside its widget
hierarchy, with [method@Gtk.Root.set_focus] and [method@Gtk.Root.get_focus].</doc>
      <source-position filename="gtk/gtkroot.h" line="34"/>
      <prerequisite name="Native"/>
      <prerequisite name="Widget"/>
      <method name="get_display" c:identifier="gtk_root_get_display">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtkroot.c"
             line="87">Returns the display that this `GtkRoot` is on.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtkroot.h" line="37"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk/gtkroot.c"
               line="93">the display of @root</doc>
          <type name="Gdk.Display" c:type="GdkDisplay*"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtkroot.c"
                 line="89">a `GtkRoot`</doc>
            <type name="Root" c:type="GtkRoot*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="get_focus" c:identifier="gtk_root_get_focus">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtkroot.c"
             line="142">Retrieves the current focused widget within the root.

Note that this is the widget that would have the focus
if the root is active; if the root is not focused then
`gtk_widget_has_focus (widget)` will be %FALSE for the
widget.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtkroot.h" line="43"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none" nullable="1">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk/gtkroot.c"
               line="153">the currently focused widget</doc>
          <type name="Widget" c:type="GtkWidget*"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtkroot.c"
                 line="144">a `GtkRoot`</doc>
            <type name="Root" c:type="GtkRoot*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="set_focus" c:identifier="gtk_root_set_focus">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtkroot.c"
             line="117">If @focus is not the current focus widget, and is focusable, sets
it as the focus widget for the root.

If @focus is %NULL, unsets the focus widget for the root.

To set the focus to a particular widget in the root, it is usually
more convenient to use [method@Gtk.Widget.grab_focus] instead of
this function.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtkroot.h" line="40"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtkroot.c"
                 line="119">a `GtkRoot`</doc>
            <type name="Root" c:type="GtkRoot*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
          <parameter name="focus"
                     transfer-ownership="none"
                     nullable="1"
                     allow-none="1">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtkroot.c"
                 line="120">widget to be the new focus widget, or %NULL
   to unset the focus widget</doc>
            <type name="Widget" c:type="GtkWidget*"/>
          </parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
    </interface>
