        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtkwidget.c"
             line="10518">Finds the descendant of the widget closest to a point.

The point (x, y) must be given in widget coordinates, so (0, 0)
is assumed to be the top left of @widget's content area.

Usually widgets will return `NULL` if the given coordinate is not
contained in @widget checked via [method@Gtk.Widget.contains].
Otherwise they will recursively try to find a child that does
not return `NULL`. Widgets are however free to customize their
picking algorithm.

This function is used on the toplevel to determine the widget
below the mouse cursor for purposes of hover highlighting and
delivering events.</doc>
